"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. The surgical pathology report indicates a Gleason 3+3 (ISUP grade group 1) and pT2c stage with no extraprostatic extension and positive surgical margins. The absence of seminal vesicle invasion and lymphovascular invasion is favorable. However, the lack of documented nodal status, as no lymph nodes were removed, widens the uncertainty regarding potential nodal involvement. Preoperative PSA was 4.0.\n\nCountervailing findings include the positive surgical margins and the missing biopsy grade/ISUP report, which introduce uncertainty regarding the true extent of the disease. The missing previous notes prevent a complete assessment of postoperative PSA trajectory. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and their subsequent trajectory is crucial for refining this prognosis. The current heuristic horizon suggests a follow-up period of approximately 51 months without an event, though the uncertainty interval spans from 31 to 72 months. Missing nodal sampling further complicates the assessment of local control. The fixed estimated horizon is 51.16 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 30.70–71.63 months; its coverage has not been validated."
